  </p>

  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    Between fluctuating gas prices hovering around $3.50 per gallon nationally, complex utility Time-of-Use (TOU) electricity tariffs, and commercial Supercharger fees, calculating your true fuel expenditure can feel overwhelming. Dealership salespeople often claim EVs run on "almost free power," while online skeptics point to expensive public fast chargers to argue that savings have vanished.
  </p>

